    {
      "card_ids": ["C01"],
      "claim": "SC-4453, a cardiac glycoside, had the lowest brain concentration (1.2 ng/g) among tissues in guinea-pigs, demonstrating a BBB to this glycoside.",
      "evidence_role": "supportive"
    },
    {
      "card_ids": ["C07"],
      "claim": "Emodin-8-O-β-D-glucoside, an anthraquinone glycoside, distributed into rat brain tissue, but its smaller size and lack of an amino sugar limit transferability to the query.",
      "evidence_role": "contradictory"
    }
  ],
  "confidence": "moderate",
  "decision_summary": "The query is an anthracycline-like glycoside with extreme polarity (logD -1.93, TPSA 206 Å², almost complete ionization) and multiple H-bond donors/acceptors. Strong negative analogues from glycosylated polycyclic natural products (digitoxin, SC-4453, mithramycin) show poor brain penetration. Positive analogues are smaller and less polar, and cyclosporine co-treatment cannot overcome the lack of passive permeability. Prediction: fail.",
